        "text": "Step 2: For \\( f(x) = 0 \\):\n- If \\( x \\leq 3 \\), then \\( f(x) = 3 - x \\). Setting this equal to 0 gives \\( 3 - x = 0 \\), so \\( x = 3 \\).\n- If \\( x > 3 \\), then \\( f(x) = -x^3 + 2x^2 + 3x \\). Setting this equal to 0 gives \\( -x^3 + 2x^2 + 3x = 0 \\). Factoring out \\( x \\) gives \\( x(-x^2 + 2x + 3) = 0 \\). This equation has solutions \\( x = 0 \\) (which is not in the domain \\( x > 3 \\)), and the quadratic equation \\( -x^2 + 2x + 3 = 0 \\). Solving the quadratic equation using the quadratic formula \\( x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \\) with \\( a = -1 \\), \\( b = 2 \\), and \\( c = 3 \\) gives \\( x = \\frac{-2 \\pm \\sqrt{4 + 12}}{-2} = \\frac{-2 \\pm 4}{-2} \\). So, \\( x = -1 \\) (not in the domain \\( x > 3 \\)) or \\( x = 3 \\) (already considered)."
