        "text": "Step 3: For \\( f(x) = 6 \\):\n- If \\( x \\leq 3 \\), then \\( f(x) = 3 - x \\). Setting this equal to 6 gives \\( 3 - x = 6 \\), so \\( x = -3 \\).\n- If \\( x > 3 \\), then \\( f(x) = -x^3 + 2x^2 + 3x \\). Setting this equal to 6 gives \\( -x^3 + 2x^2 + 3x = 6 \\). Rearranging terms gives \\( -x^3 + 2x^2 + 3x - 6 = 0 \\). Testing possible rational roots, we find that \\( x = 2 \\) is a root because \\( -(2)^3 + 2(2)^2 + 3(2) - 6 = -8 + 8 + 6 - 6 = 0 \\). Therefore, \\( x = 2 \\) is not in the domain \\( x > 3 \\), so we need to check other possible roots. By synthetic division or further factorization, we can confirm that there are no other real roots greater than 3."
